{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-413817-r4629250","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Chocolate Cake with Coconut Topping (Vegan)","sourcePageId":413817,"sourceRevision":"4629250","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-05T01:27:47Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Acrions","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Chocolate%20Cake%20with%20Coconut%20Topping%20(Vegan)&oldid=4629250","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:38:11.334Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cake","Category:Recipes using apple","Category:Recipes using cocoa powder","Category:Recipes using coconut","Category:Recipes using dark chocolate","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using lemon zest","Category:Recipes using lingonberry","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using soy flour","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Vegan recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"61a8b45abb5cd270dda7fa65cbe0fea72dc7b5743086da81bdb4707468b5af26","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Cake recipes|servings=2|time=40 minutes|difficulty=1|Image=}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Vegan cuisine|Vegan Cuisine]]\n\nThis recipe is for a vegan chocolate cake with a coconut crumble topping.\n\n==Ingredients==\n=== Wet ingredients ===\n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]], very soft\n* 400 g white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 75 g dried grated [[Cookbook:Coconut|coconut]]\n* [[Cookbook:Zest|Zest]] of a [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] or grated [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 250 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Soy Milk|soy milk]], cold\n\n=== Dry ingredients ===\n* 750 g [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|flour]]\n* 150 g [[Cookbook:Soy Flour|soy flour]]\n* 2 sachets (40 g) [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinches]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]] powder\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 2 teaspoons salt\n* 100 g unsweetened [[Cookbook:Cocoa Powder|cocoa powder]]\n\n=== Add-ins ===\n''Either:''\n* 450 ml soy milk\n* 2 glasses (500 g) [[Cookbook:Cranberry|cranberries]] or [[Cookbook:Lingonberry|lingonberries]]\n\n''or:''\n* 700 ml soy milk\n* 2 small [[Cookbook:Apple|apples]], cut into small pieces\n\n=== Topping ===\n\n* 200 g dark [[Cookbook:Chocolate|chocolate]] couverture\n* Grated coconut\n\n== Procedure ==\n# [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] all wet ingredients together for 10 minutes until creamy, adding the soy milk gradually to the other ingredients.\n# Combine all dry ingredients, then [[Cookbook:Sifting|sift]] loosely to aerate and remove lumps.\n# Preheat the [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 200°C.\n# Add the wet mixture and the add-ins to the dry mixture. Stir briefly until smooth. Do not over-mix, since this will cause the [[Cookbook:Batter|batter]] to deflate and become tough.\n# Spread the batter in a large [[Cookbook:Baking Pan|baking pan]] lined with [[Cookbook:Parchment Paper|baking paper]].\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 20 minutes. Turn off the oven, and let the cake continue cooking in the residual heat for 15 minutes. Let cool.\n# Unmold the cake from the pan, and remove the baking paper.\n# Melt the chocolate couverture over a [[Cookbook:Double Boiler|double boiler]]. Spread the melted chocolate on top of the cake, then sprinkle with grated coconut.\n# Sprinkle the still soft couverture with grated coconut.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Do not overmix the batter once the wet and dry mixtures have been combined. This will prematurely release all the CO<sub>2</sub> and make the cake tough.\n* The cake becomes greasy if it contains too much margarine relative to the other ingredients. Margarine is heavy and does not give stability (unlike flour).\n* The cake can collapse if you take it out of the oven too early. If you wait too long, it gets too dry or even burns. If you wait too short or if the baking temperature is too low, it will not be cooked through.\n* The detailed recipe version is available on the homepage of [[User:Mamue|Markus Müller]]: http://www.mm65.de/VeganerSchokoladenkuchen.html (German).\n\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for cake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cocoa powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using soy flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon zest]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lingonberry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chocolate Cake with Coconut Topping (Vegan)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"200 g margarine, very soft","sourceText":"200 g margarine, very soft","amountText":"200 g margarine, very soft","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"400 g white granulated sugar","sourceText":"400 g white granulated sugar","amountText":"400 g white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"75 g dried grated coconut","sourceText":"75 g dried grated coconut","amountText":"75 g dried grated coconut","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Zest of a lemon or grated ginger","sourceText":"Zest of a lemon or grated ginger","amountText":"Zest of a lemon or grated ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"250 ml soy milk, cold","sourceText":"250 ml soy milk, cold","amountText":"250 ml soy milk, cold","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"750 g flour","sourceText":"750 g flour","amountText":"750 g flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"150 g soy flour","sourceText":"150 g soy flour","amountText":"150 g soy flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 sachets (40 g) baking powder","sourceText":"2 sachets (40 g) baking powder","amountText":"2 sachets (40 g) baking powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"6 pinches vanilla powder","sourceText":"6 pinches vanilla powder","amountText":"6 pinches vanilla powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 teaspoon cinnamon","sourceText":"1 teaspoon cinnamon","amountText":"1 teaspoon cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"2 teaspoons salt","sourceText":"2 teaspoons salt","amountText":"2 teaspoons salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-12","name":"100 g unsweetened cocoa powder","sourceText":"100 g unsweetened cocoa powder","amountText":"100 g unsweetened cocoa powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-13","name":"450 ml soy milk","sourceText":"450 ml soy milk","amountText":"450 ml soy milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-14","name":"2 glasses (500 g) cranberries or lingonberries","sourceText":"2 glasses (500 g) cranberries or lingonberries","amountText":"2 glasses (500 g) cranberries or lingonberries","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-15","name":"700 ml soy milk","sourceText":"700 ml soy milk","amountText":"700 ml soy milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-16","name":"2 small apples, cut into small pieces","sourceText":"2 small apples, cut into small pieces","amountText":"2 small apples, cut into small pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-17","name":"200 g dark chocolate couverture","sourceText":"200 g dark chocolate couverture","amountText":"200 g dark chocolate couverture","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-18","name":"Grated coconut","sourceText":"Grated coconut","amountText":"Grated coconut","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Beat all wet ingredients together for 10 minutes until creamy, adding the soy milk gradually to the other ingredients.","sourceText":"Beat all wet ingredients together for 10 minutes until creamy, adding the soy milk gradually to the other ingredients.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Combine all dry ingredients, then sift loosely to aerate and remove lumps.","sourceText":"Combine all dry ingredients, then sift loosely to aerate and remove lumps.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Preheat the oven to 200°C.","sourceText":"Preheat the oven to 200°C.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Add the wet mixture and the add-ins to the dry mixture. Stir briefly until smooth. Do not over-mix, since this will cause the batter to deflate and become tough.","sourceText":"Add the wet mixture and the add-ins to the dry mixture. Stir briefly until smooth. Do not over-mix, since this will cause the batter to deflate and become tough.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Spread the batter in a large baking pan lined with